metadata:
  name: Sorbetto di Lamponi
  images:
    - empty.png
  description: "Italian Raspberry Sorbet. A classic Italian-style sorbet — pure raspberry flavor, silky texture, no dairy or eggs."
  notes: "Needs an ice cream machine. The base must be fully chilled before churning."
  types: [Dessert, Ice Cream]
  estimatedPrepTime: 30 min + 4 h
  servings: 6

ingredients:
 - 550 g fresh raspberries
 - 160 g granulated sugar
 - 120 ml water
 - 1 tbsp freshly squeezed lemon juice
 - 0.1 tsp fine salt

actions:
 - divider Make the base
 - free_text <b>Make the syrup:</b> Combine 160 g granulated sugar and 120 ml water in a small saucepan. Warm over medium heat, stirring, just until the sugar fully dissolves — no need to boil. Remove from heat and let cool.
 - free_text <b>Purée the raspberries:</b> Blend 550 g fresh raspberries until completely smooth, about 30–60 seconds.
 - free_text <b>Strain out the seeds:</b> Push the purée through a fine-mesh sieve with a spatula or the back of a ladle, pressing well to extract all the pulp. Discard the seeds. This is what gives Italian sorbetto its silky texture — don't skip it.
 - free_text <b>Combine the base:</b> Stir the cooled syrup into the raspberry purée along with 1 tbsp freshly squeezed lemon juice and 0.1 tsp fine salt. Taste — it should seem slightly too sweet at room temperature, since cold dulls sweetness.
 - divider Chill, churn and freeze
 - free_text <b>Chill thoroughly:</b> Refrigerate the base until completely cold, at least 120 minutes (or overnight). A cold base churns faster and gives smaller ice crystals.
 - free_text <b>Churn:</b> Pour the base into your ice cream machine and churn until it reaches a thick, soft-serve consistency, typically 20–25 minutes depending on the machine.
 - free_text <b>Firm up in the freezer:</b> Transfer to a chilled, lidded container, press a piece of parchment against the surface, and freeze until scoopable, about 120 minutes. Let it sit at room temperature for 5 minutes before serving if it's been frozen longer.
